source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Print the version of snouty, and the git commit that it was built from.

The commit is the short hash of the commit, with a `-dirty` suffix when the
build had uncommitted changes. A build from a source tarball has no commit.

Examples:
  snouty version

Add --json for machine-readable output. The version prints as one JSON object,
with the fields version and commit. commit is null when the build has no commit:
  snouty --json version | jq -r .version

Usage: snouty version [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --utc
          Show times in UTC instead of the local timezone

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
